Problem: (r5) the dark theme used dark-grey surfaces (#1d1b1f / #312f33 / #42414d etc.), not true black, so AMOLED pixels stay lit. (r6) after the r5 remap, the Settings page became a pure-black void: androidx.preference rows are transparent ripples on the fragment backdrop (colorBackground = fx_mobile_background = #000000), and its list dividers are #1f000000 (invisible on black) — the whole page read as an empty black screen.
Root cause: values-night/colors.xml maps the Material3 surface tokens to novaGray65-85 (dark greys) and layer tokens to photonDarkGrey30/80 — none are #000000, so AMOLED pixels stay on (r5). The r6 settings void is caused by the preference stack itself: androidx.preference 1.2.1 paints no row background (Preference styleable has no android:background; preference_material.xml root uses only a transparent selectableItemBackground ripple), PreferenceFragmentCompat renders rows over the activity colorBackground, and its divider drawable is #1f000000 — all structure carriers vanished once the backdrop became #000000.
Affected layer: app UI resources only (values-night/colors.xml, values/styles.xml, drawable/, layout/). No Kotlin, no GeckoView, no build config.
Implementation: keep the true-black AMOLED base (background/surface/dim = #000000) and lift the container scale off pure black so elevation hierarchy is preserved and lowest-tier surfaces stay distinguishable (lowest #0A0A0A < low #121212 < container #1A1A1A < high #1F1F1F < highest #242424; surface_variant #161616; search layer_color_3 #141414). Fix the settings void at the source: preference rows now render on an inset rounded card (@layout/op7_preference_row + @drawable/op7_preference_row_background, fill ?attr/colorSurfaceContainer = #1A1A1A, same as home cards) via PreferenceTheme.preferenceStyle and SwitchCompatPreferenceMaterialStyle; androidx list dividers are neutralized (transparent) so full-width lines don't cross the card gaps. Card rows are visible on the black backdrop while home/chrome stays AMOLED-black.
Expected benefit: AMOLED panel power saving proportional to lit-pixel reduction on UI chrome (toolbar, menus, dialogs, home) plus a usable, premium settings page: visible card rows on a pure-black backdrop, consistent with the home screen. Measurable via screen-on drain deltas and pixel-coverage screenshots (before/after).
Benchmark: r5 baseline in docs/performance/ (black-pixel coverage + screen-on mA method). r6 target: settings page no longer a void (visual QA) + no regression in r5 black-pixel coverage on home/chrome. No frame-time claim.
Regression risk: cosmetic/theme only; text contrast preserved (on-surface stays near-white #f2f0f8). Card row layout is a pinned copy of androidx.preference 1.2.1 preference_material — upstream bump that changes that layout will surface as a patch conflict and stop the pipeline (by design). Light theme untouched. Revert = drop patch.
Upstream relationship: not for upstream (device-specific AMOLED preference + settings visibility); Fenix deliberately uses Material dark greys and flat preference rows. Could be proposed as an optional AMOLED toggle later.

